# Prettier is the constitution's TS/JS formatter (spec 095). It is checked by the `lint` targets of
# mcm-app and design-system, which run, from the project directory:
#
#   prettier --check --ignore-path ../../.prettierignore '**/*.{ts,tsx,js,mjs}'
#
# Use that invocation (with --write) to format. Do NOT run a bare `prettier --write .` from the repo
# root: Prettier also reads the root .gitignore, and matches it CASE-INSENSITIVELY where git does
# not. The Visual Studio rule `Backup*/` there therefore hides every `backups/` directory from
# Prettier while git still tracks it — 14 mcm-app files were silently skipped that way. Passing
# --ignore-path replaces .gitignore with this file, so the check sees them.
#
# This file excludes the projects' generated and vendored output.
node_modules
dist
build
coverage
.expo
android
ios
web-build
playwright-report
test-results
*.snap
